<document source="specs/hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md" type="spec" relevance="0.50" tokens="795">
## The run

- `ChatOrchestrator.processMessageStream` takes an optional second argument, `{signal}`, and hands the signal to `provider.sendMessage` as `params.signal`, the very object the caller passed ([validated by: reaches the provider as params.signal, the very object the caller passed @b27310ea](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L720)).
- A run whose provider stops on the abort ends with that round: `afterModelResponse` does not fire, since there is no finished answer, and `afterSession` fires once ([validated by: skips afterModelResponse when its provider stops on the abort, firing afterSession once @31ac7c27](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L739)).
- An abort is a controlled stop, not a failure: a failure after the signal aborted ends the run quietly, with no `onError`, no `afterModelResponse`, since there is no finished response, and no rethrow, while `afterSession` fires once ([validated by: ends quietly when the provider fails after the signal aborted: no onError, afterModelResponse or rethrow, afterSession once @21652c16](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L745)).
- Each tool call's `ToolContext.signal` is composed from the run's signal and the call's own through `AbortSignal.any`, so neither replaces the other: abandoning the run aborts it, and so does the call's deadline ([validated by: aborts each call's context signal when its run is abandoned, the signal still the call's own @7c4e10eb](../../src/toolDeadline.test.ts#L384), [validated by: answers a call that never settles at toolTimeoutMs with a result naming the tool and the deadline, and aborts its signal @059f9ce2](../../src/toolDeadline.test.ts#L100)).
- A round whose run is abandoned while a tool hangs ends at once, with a deadline or with `toolTimeoutMs: 0`, and no provider call follows it ([validated by: ends the round at once when its run is abandoned while a tool hangs, with a deadline or with none @8658af2c](../../src/toolDeadline.test.ts#L394)).
- A round leaves no listener on the run's signal once its calls have settled, so a long-lived connection does not collect one per tool call ([validated by: leaves no abort listener on the run signal once its calls have settled @b2bf1da1](../../src/toolDeadline.test.ts#L404)).
- Nothing a round produced is recorded once its run is abandoned, not even an entry a tool that finished first asked the client to show, and the provider is asked nothing more ([validated by: records nothing the round produced once its run is abandoned, and asks the provider nothing more @5746280b](../../src/toolDeadline.test.ts#L414)).
- `withRetry` composes the run's signal with each attempt's own rather than replacing it, so an abort reaches the attempt in flight, and its own timeouts still abort an attempt when no signal is passed ([validated by: composes a caller signal with each attempt signal, so a caller abort reaches the provider while its stream is live @cd2ab319](../../src/providers/withRetry.test.ts#L58), [validated by: abandons an attempt whose first chunk never arrives, aborts its signal, calls return on it, and retries @6bbf6830](../../src/providers/withRetry.test.ts#L173)).
</document>
<document source="specs/hal-engine-before-tool-call-hook/spec.md" type="spec" relevance="0.49" tokens="208">
## A policy that throws

- A throwing policy declines its call rather than ending the conversation: the executor does not run, the model receives a `tool_result` naming the tool, `stream_end` is sent, `afterModelResponse` fires once, and `onError` does not fire, because the turn did not fail ([validated by: declines the call when the policy throws, and the turn survives with every hook but onError @1d3a5b02](../../src/transport/ws/beforeToolCall.test.ts#L180)).
- Every `tool_use` block the provider was sent must be answered by a `tool_result`, so a raw throw escaping the round would leave the conversation unanswerable; catching it keeps the turn alive ([validated by: declines the call when the policy throws, and the turn survives with every hook but onError @1d3a5b02](../../src/transport/ws/beforeToolCall.test.ts#L180)).
</document>
<document source="specs/hal-engine-session-write-signal/spec.md" type="spec" relevance="0.48" tokens="236">
## When it fails

- **NIS-2 Article 21.** A `save` that rejects does not fail the turn: the caller still receives the answer, and the failure becomes exactly one logged line under category `orchestrator`, message `session save failed`, carrying the session id and the error's message ([validated by: keeps the turn alive and logs once when save rejects @bbdb399c](../../src/orchestration/sessionSave.test.ts#L48)).
- A `save` that throws synchronously is handled identically, so an implementation that forgets to be async cannot take the turn down ([validated by: keeps the turn alive when save throws synchronously @28642d2c](../../src/orchestration/sessionSave.test.ts#L57)).
- An `afterSession` hook that throws does not cost the turn its write signal: `save` still fires, and the hook's error still reaches the caller ([validated by: saves even when an afterSession hook throws @d4b4db54](../../src/orchestration/sessionSave.test.ts#L73)).
</document>
<document source="specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md" type="spec" relevance="0.47" tokens="788">
## Emission

- `sendStreamEnd` has one call site in `messageHandler.ts`, reached from the `finally` of each turn the handler runs, so a throw anywhere in the run still reaches it unless the turn's socket closed first ([abandon-on-close](../hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md)); `handleUserMessage` sends none ([validated by: ends a provider failure mid-stream with error then stream_end, stream_end last @06dbc5a6](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L391)).
- A run failing mid-stream, after the answer has started, produces `error` then `stream_end`, with `stream_end` the last frame ([validated by: ends a provider failure mid-stream with error then stream_end, stream_end last @06dbc5a6](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L391)).
- A provider rate limit produces `error` (`RATE_LIMITED`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: tells the client to retry when the provider is rate limited @2d9ce92b](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L372)).
- Any other failure, one that is no `AIError`, produces `error` (`SERVER_ERROR`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: reports any other failure as a server error @0bc6f4b6](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L381)).
- A `user_message` that fails validation (empty, blank or over-length content) never reaches the orchestrator and still produces `error` (`INVALID_MESSAGE`) then `stream_end` ([validated by: answers an empty user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end @ed14278a](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L415), [validated by: answers a blank user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end @b5f26f9c](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L419), [validated by: answers an over-length user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end @3729fd89](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L423)).
- A malformed `ping` produces `error` (`INVALID_MESSAGE`) and no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a malformed ping with INVALID_MESSAGE and no stream_end @c6190929](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L427)).
- A valid `ping` produces `pong` and no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a ping with the timestamp it was given @92823c22](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L82)).
- A malformed `ping` arriving mid-run gets its own `error` frame, the run's deltas continue unaffected, and exactly one `stream_end` is the very last frame ([validated by: keeps one stream_end, last, when a malformed ping lands mid-run @ab4381dc](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L435)).
- A three-round tool conversation still produces exactly one `stream_end`, as its last frame ([validated by: sends one stream_end for a three-round tool conversation @4033b2b6](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L456)).
- Unparseable JSON is rejected before the server can tell what frame type it was meant to be, so it produces `error` (`INVALID_FORMAT`) alone and is never dispatched; this is the one case in which a client falls back on the socket closing ([validated by: answers unparseable JSON with INVALID_FORMAT alone and never dispatches it @7f9a339b](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L239)).
</document>
